        <mxCell id="n34" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n16" target="n17"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n35" value="COMMIT" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n17" target="n18"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n36" value="yes" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n18" target="n19"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n37" value="no" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n18" target="n20"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n38" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n19" target="n21"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n39" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n19" target="n20"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1120" y="1210"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n40" value="A — Bug found while drawing this.  orders.service.ts:544 and :621&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;cancel() and cancelSale() both wrap the refund call in try/catch and only&lt;br&gt;console.error the failure — then save the order as cancelled anyway. If the&lt;br&gt;refund throws, the buyer money stays in escrow_hold forever and nothing&lt;br&gt;raises an alarm.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;escrows.refund() itself is correct: one transaction, idempotency key&lt;br&gt;escrow_refund:{id}. The defect is the caller swallowing what it throws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The red frame is what SHOULD be one transaction. Today it is three separate&lt;br&gt;writes, so a crash between them leaves the order cancelled with the stock&lt;br&gt;still gone, or the stock back with the money never returned." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#c8a415;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1340" width="800" height="210" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n41" value="B — Bug found while drawing this.  nobody voids the PayOS link&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;orders.cancel() never calls payos.cancelPaymentLink(), so cancelling an&lt;br&gt;UNPAID order leaves the payment link live. payos.service.ts:486 then sets&lt;br&gt;status = CONFIRMED on webhook without checking the current status.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;So: cancel an unpaid order, pay the old link, and the cancelled order comes&lt;br&gt;back to life as confirmed — while its stock was already returned to the shelf.&lt;br&gt;The red box is the missing half; a status check in the webhook is the other." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#c8a415;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="880" y="1340" width="800" height="210" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
